{
  "AboutDemo": {
    "title": "About this demo",
    "subtitle": "This is a portfolio deployment. The platform manages real PostgreSQL instances — but a fresh fleet of empty databases for fictional companies has nothing to monitor. So the demo generates a believable, living fleet on purpose, and this page is upfront about exactly what is real and what is generated.",
    "real": {
      "title": "What is real",
      "body": "Six PostgreSQL 16 containers, provisioned and managed by this platform, each with data loaded. Everything the dashboard measures — connections, throughput, latency, slow queries, disk growth, backups (pg_dump), VACUUM/ANALYZE — runs against these real databases. No number on screen is faked."
    },
    "generated": {
      "title": "What is generated",
      "body": "The three companies and their users are fictional. A light, continuous synthetic load keeps the fleet alive — its connections identify themselves as 'dbaas-demo-workload' in the active-connections screen, never disguised as user traffic. And 24h of metrics, 30-day uptime, weeks of backups, alerts and maintenance history are seeded at startup, because a KPI like 30-day uptime cannot happen in a five-minute visit."
    },
    "howItWorks": {
      "title": "How it stays alive",
      "body": "On boot, the seed provisions the fleet, loads data, and writes the historical baseline. From then on a background generator keeps a gentle base load flowing, following a realistic daily curve. So the moment you log in, the platform already looks and behaves like a fleet under management — no button to press, no empty first screen."
    },
    "decision": {
      "title": "Why there is no “Simulate usage” button",
      "body": "An earlier version gated all of this behind a “Simulate usage” button: a clean clone booted empty, and one click ran a scripted ~90-second demo (traffic climbing, an alert firing, a backup and maintenance running). It was honest, but the first screen looked switched off and most visitors never clicked. So the idea was folded into the product itself — the fleet is now generated and kept alive from the first second, and this notice keeps that transparent. A monitoring platform should be shown monitoring something."
    }
  },
